-- title:
--   Switcheroo Aggregate Once Commuted Scalar Point
-- statement:
--   **The once-commuted scalar admits an equivalent product-type sum.**
--
--   For a fixed slice-pair question `q`, the sum over a polynomial `g` and outcome `o` of the complete-part total followed by the `M` and family factors equals the sum over the paired type `Polynomial params x Outcome`. Writing $C_q$ for the complete-part total, $M_q(o)$ for the `M` outcome, and $G_q(g)$ for the family outcome, the identity is
--
--   $$
--   \sum_g\sum_o\operatorname{ev}_{\psi_{bi}}(\operatorname{leftTensor}(C_qM_q(o)G_q(g)M_q(o)G_q(g)))
--   =\sum_{(g,o)}\operatorname{ev}_{\psi_{bi}}(\operatorname{leftTensor}(C_qM_q(o)G_q(g)M_q(o)G_q(g))).
--   $$
--
--   This is a finite-sum regrouping only. It exposes the product index expected by the once-commuted scalar and is used in its comparison with the mixed scalar.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.switcherooAggregateOnceCommutedScalar_point`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
